ate FUNCTION-wrapped call, nested currying, and the negative-witness boundary case), wired into tests/closeout/run.sh as a seventh gate. Adversarially confirmed: rebuilt the pre-change mccarthy-kernel.s in a scratch copy, confirmed all 5 positive fixtures genuinely fail on it, and confirmed the negative-witness fixture passes on BOTH versions (proving the boundary was narrowed, not accidentally erased). docs/S0-SEED-CONTRACT.md, README.md updated to reflect the narrowed (not closed) gap: closures now work when built via explicit FUNCTION, still don't for naked LAMBDA-as-value, matching real historical LISP 1.5 exactly.")
